ce transportation and logistics solutions in the United States, Canada, and Mexico. It operates in three segments: Truckload, Intermodal, and Logistics. The Truckload segment offers over-the-road freight transportation services through dry van, bulk, temperature-controlled, lightweight, and flatbed trailers across dedicated or network configurations. Its Intermodal segment provides door-to-door container on flat car services through a combination of rail and dray transportation using company-owned containers, chassis, and trucks. The Logistics segment offers asset-light freight brokerage, supply chain, warehousing, and import/export services, as well as value-added services. The company also leases equipment, such as trucks to owner-operators and provides insurance to drivers and owner-operators. Schneider National, Inc. was founded in 1935 and is headquartered in Green Bay, Wisconsin.","ceo_bio":"Mr. James S. Filter | CEO, President & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $716,261 (FY2022)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 19K people. Revenue per employee of $299K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $15K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $900 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Schneider National, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $5.1B market cap on $5.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -5% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $285M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 6.15\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 5.0\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.6%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 50% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (12.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $4.2M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-4185353.46},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Industrials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 34% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 37% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Why (SNDR) Price Action Is Critical for Tactical Trading","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/1/Why_SNDR_Price_Action_Is_Critical_for_Tactical_Trading_112326014803_1795459683.html","date":"2026-11-23","timestamp":1795459683.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.557,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What Is Driving Schneider National (NYSE:SNDR) Latest Performance?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/industrial/what-is-driving-schneider-national-nysesndr-latest-performance","date":"2026-11-16","timestamp":1794834840.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Trading the Move, Not the Narrative: (SNDR) Edition","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/90/Trading_the_Move,_Not_the_Narrative:_SNDR_Edition_111326032402_1794601442.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794601442.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"S&P upgrades CPKC to A- on diversified growth, Mexico-US corridor","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/p-upgrades-cpkc-diversified-growth-140148979.html","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795615308.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.931,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"3 U.S. Freight Stocks Investors May Watch as Rail Merger Pressure Grows","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/transportation/nasdaq-jbht/jb-hunt-transport-services/news/3-us-freight-stocks-investors-may-watch-as-rail-merger-press","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795565587.497,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.052,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Georgia Po